      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Coronary endarterectomy is necessary in up to 37% of patients undergoing coronary artery bypass grafting surgery. Bypass grafting of \"inoperable arteries\" allows complete revascularization, improves prognosis and quality of life of patients with diffusely diseased coronary arteries. The article considers reconstructive techniques for coronary arteries after endarterectomy."},
